Subject: [PATCH 13/13] bridge: expose live flasher script image by part

Tables whose script disables its FlexDMD stage in desktop mode (e.g. JP's
Space Cadet: UseFlexDMD=False when ShowDT=True, so no FlexDMD instance
exists) draw scores through script `Flasher.ImageA` writes on digit
flashers, so the host needs the current image name per part to mirror the
swaps. Reads `FlasherData::m_szImageA` by part index; null when no table
is loaded, the index is out of range, the part is no flasher, or its image
is empty, so the row's image state stays untouched. An empty image reads
as unknown rather than clear (upstream would render untextured); no digit
path here assigns '' (DMDDisplayChar maps '' to space, DMDUpdate guards
line 2 to bkborder). Adds one narrow getter; no script or table changes.
Rebuild with wasm/build-headless.sh.

Target: vpinball/vpinball@64a480a96d1b972711fbb8eea014654c779b1e23

diff --git a/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp b/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp
--- a/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp
+++ b/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp
@@ -87,6 +87,9 @@ CComObject<PinTable> *g_table;
 CComObject<PinTable> *g_table;
 Player *g_player;
 std::string g_catalog;
+// Scratch for VpxWasm_GetFlasherImage: the reader copies the name out before
+// the next call, same single-threaded contract as the buffer views.
+std::string g_flasherImage;
 std::vector<float> g_buf[5];
 int g_bufStride[5];
 int g_bufCount[5];
@@ -437,11 +440,31 @@ EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE const char *VpxWasm_GetScriptError()
 EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE const char *VpxWasm_GetScriptError()
 {
    if (!g_player)
       return nullptr;
    const std::string &err = g_player->GetLastScriptError();
    return err.empty() ? nullptr : err.c_str();
 }
 
+// Current script image of one flasher part. Script `Flasher.ImageA = ...`
+// writes land in `FlasherData::m_szImageA`; tables whose script disables
+// its FlexDMD stage in desktop mode drive their whole display through it,
+// so the host polls this once per flasher row per frame. Null when no
+// table is loaded, the index is out of range, the part is no flasher, or
+// its image is empty: the row's image state then stays untouched.
+EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE const char *VpxWasm_GetFlasherImage(int partIdx)
+{
+   if (!g_table || partIdx < 0)
+      return nullptr;
+   const vector<IEditable *> &parts = g_table->GetParts();
+   if ((size_t)partIdx >= parts.size())
+      return nullptr;
+   IEditable *const part = parts[(size_t)partIdx];
+   if (!part || part->GetItemType() != eItemFlasher)
+      return nullptr;
+   g_flasherImage = static_cast<Flasher *>(part)->m_d.m_szImageA;
+   return g_flasherImage.empty() ? nullptr : g_flasherImage.c_str();
+}
